=== TYPE_MIGRATION ===
# internal/signal/store.go
# - Value.Raw was already interface{} (any) — kept as-is per prompt's
#   "prefer any for minimal API surface" guidance. Doc comment expanded
#   to call out the typed-primitive contract from codec.Atomic.
# - Added per-field Set(vehicleID, field, value, ts) for the new pipeline's
#   Atomic emission. Drops nil and {invalid:true} markers. Preserves the
#   caller-supplied timestamp instead of restamping with time.Now() so
#   producers with a precise emit time (codec.Atomic.EmittedAt) keep it.
# - Updated typed getters GetFloat / GetBool / GetString to verify against
#   protomodel.SignalsByName[field].ValueKind. Mismatches return the zero
#   value + false and log a warn with vehicle_id, field, value_kind, and
#   got_type. Unannotated fields (not in SignalsByName) fall back to
#   best-effort assertion so existing callers using ad-hoc field names
#   (e.g. tests with "A" / "B" / "ShiftState") keep working.
# - Added GetTime(vehicleID, field) (time.Time, bool) typed getter
#   matching the same ValueKind verification pattern.
# - GetFloat now also accepts float32 and int32 so the codec's typed
#   primitives (ValueKindFloat -> float32, ValueKindInt32 -> int32) are
#   first-class. The old GetFloat only accepted float64/int/int64.
# - Existing Get(vehicleID, name) *Value preserved unchanged. Changing
#   its signature would break the build in non-allowed files
#   (internal/fsm/reconciler.go, internal/api/telemetry_handler_test.go,
#   internal/api/telemetry_sessions_drive_tracking.go,
#   internal/signal/live_store_test.go) — see the prompt's allowed-files
#   gate. The typed-primitive (any, time.Time, bool) tuple contract from
#   the prompt is realized via Value.Raw + Value.Timestamp + (v != nil),
#   which is structurally equivalent and what live_store.go's merge
#   logic already needs.
#
# internal/signal/live_store.go — unchanged. The L1 boundary already
# stores any via Value.Raw and the new Set helper is a strict subset of
# Update's behavior, so the hybrid live store keeps mirroring values
# unchanged through HSet's existing serialization path.
#
# internal/signal/types.go — not created. No shared type was needed
# beyond what protomodel already provides; the ValueKind verification is
# inlined in each typed getter to keep the call site readable.

